# OS junk
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# Rust build artifacts
**/target/
**/Cargo.lock

# Tauri generated files
desktop/app/src-tauri/gen/

# Node
**/node_modules/

# VibeExtract replication output (scratch screenshots, logs)
.replica-output/
# Playwright MCP scratch (browser snapshots + console logs from the dev tool)
.playwright-mcp/
replica-*.png
*-output.html
*-output.toon
*-output.png
combo-output.*
native-output.*

# .replicate-ui/ is PURE SCRATCH — per-extraction working dirs + generated replica
# outputs (index.html, harvested assets, captures, sprite cache) + local per-app dev
# examples. The reusable toolkit now lives INSIDE the skill
# (.claude/skills/replicate-ui/_shared/), so nothing here needs tracking; deleting
# the whole folder loses nothing but caching speed.
.replicate-ui/

# Skill toolkit: ship the source, but ignore generated artifacts —
# the compiled Vision OCR + catalog-extract binaries (rebuilt on first use) and Python caches.
.claude/skills/replicate-ui/_shared/vision_ocr
.claude/skills/replicate-ui/_shared/catalog_extract
**/__pycache__/

# Generated Tauri icon set — regenerate with `cargo tauri icon` (build-dmg.sh does
# this). The .icns/.ico/platform dirs aren't committed; the source icon.png is.
desktop/app/src-tauri/icons/*.icns
desktop/app/src-tauri/icons/*.ico
desktop/app/src-tauri/icons/android/
desktop/app/src-tauri/icons/ios/

# Claude Code local settings (shared commands/skills stay committable)
# .claude/settings.local.json

# Scratch PNGs anywhere — but keep the source app icon.
*.png
!desktop/app/src-tauri/icons/icon.png
*.otf
*preview.html